==> Intel CPU built-in accelerators...
  ok: AMX (amx_bf16 amx_int8 amx_tile) — CPU instructions, usable in any pod; up labels nodes feature.node.kubernetes.io/cpu-cpuid.AMX*
  ok: CPU ISA: AVX512BF16 AVX512F AVX512VNNI — up labels nodes feature.node.kubernetes.io/cpu-cpuid.<name>=true (NFD names)
  ok: DSA: 2 device(s), 1 user work queue(s) — deployed by 'k3d-gpu up' (intel-dsa-plugin); pods need CAP_SYS_RAWIO to mmap a WQ portal (INTEL-SA-01084)
  ok: IAA: 2 device(s), 1 user work queue(s) — deployed by 'k3d-gpu up' (intel-iaa-plugin); pods need CAP_SYS_RAWIO to mmap a WQ portal (INTEL-SA-01084)
  ok: QAT 0000:6b:00.0 (4xxx): 4 VF(s) — deployed by 'k3d-gpu up' (intel-qat-plugin binds them to vfio-pci)
  ok: NUMA: 2 node(s) (2 with CPUs), SNC 1 per L3, 2 socket(s) — up deploys the NRI balloons policy; label pods k3d-gpu.io/cores=replica for a balloon inside one NUMA node, memory pinned to it, near the pod's devices
  info: RDT allocation (rdt_a: cat_l3 cdp_l3 mba) — resctrl classes are available but left off: the balloons policy ships control.rdt.enable: false because enabling it rewrites the host's /sys/fs/resctrl. To opt in, mount resctrl on the host (mount -t resctrl resctrl /sys/fs/resctrl) and set control.rdt.enable: true in nri-balloons.yml; usePodQoSAsDefaultClass then gives BestEffort/Burstable/Guaranteed pods 33%/66%/100% of the L3. To revert, set control.rdt.enable: false in nri-balloons.yml, then sudo umount /sys/fs/resctrl
  info: noisy-neighbour isolation: rdt-mba — CAT + MBA can cap a neighbour's cache share and DRAM bandwidth through the RDT opt-in above (resctrl mounted: no); the shipped classes set cache shares only, so add mbAllocation: {all: ["50%"]} to the BestEffort class for bandwidth; the classes run inside the NRI balloons policy, which up deploys on hybrid or multi-NUMA hosts only
  info: per socket: socket 0: DSA 1, IAA 1, QAT 1; socket 1: DSA 1, IAA 1, QAT 0 (ARK default for 8480+: DSA 1, IAA 1, QAT 1 per socket)
  warn: socket 1: QAT 0 below the ARK default for 8480+ — the BIOS may have the device disabled; check its accelerator settings
  info: Intel On Demand interface present (intel_vsec.sdsi.0, intel_vsec.sdsi.1): on On Demand SKUs, instances above the ARK default are activated by a license (https://github.com/intel/intel-sdsi); ask the platform vendor whether activation is offered
